        <dc:title>Children of the Corn</dc:title>
        <dc:creator opf:file-as="King, Stephen" opf:role="aut">Stephen King</dc:creator>
        <dc:contributor opf:file-as="calibre" opf:role="bkp">calibre (8.14.0) [https://calibre-ebook.com]</dc:contributor>
        <dc:date>1977-03-01T05:00:00+00:00</dc:date>
        <dc:description>&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From the unrivaled master of horror and the supernatural, Stephen King •  “Children of the Corn,” first collected in the extraordinary collection Night Shift in 1973 and then adapted into a horror film franchise of the same name, is a terrifying and unforgettable classic of the genre. Driving through the cornfields in rural Nebraska, Burt and Vicky run over a young boy—only to discover that they may not be responsible for his death. Out in the corn, something is watching them, and help is nowhere to be found. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A Vintage Short.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</dc:description>
